      "components": ["U10", "U5"],
      "pins": ["U10.5", "U10.6", "U10.7", "U10.8", "U5.7", "U5.9", "U5.10", "U5.17"],
      "nets": ["NET0003", "NET0053", "NET0021", "NET0030"],
      "observed": "All five keyboard column outputs are connected to SKW92A pins identified by the netlist as LAN_PORT1 Ethernet PHY signals. For example, NET0003 joins U10.5 LAN_PORT1_TX+ to U5.7 COL1; NET0053 joins U10.6 LAN_PORT1_TX- to U5.9 COL2; NET0021 and NET0030 similarly connect LAN_PORT1_RX+/- to keyboard columns.",
      "expected": "The specification says the keyboard matrix lines are wired directly to SKW92A GPIO pins. Keyboard column signals should use GPIO-capable pins and remain separate from Ethernet PHY signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0003\") ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_TX+\")) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"COL1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0053\") ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_TX-\")) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"COL2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0021\") ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_RX+\")) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"10\") (pinfunction \"COL3\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0030\") ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_RX-\")) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"17\") (pinfunction \"COL4\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "netlist shows 5 column + 7 row lines wired directly to SKW92A GPIO pins (matrix scanned by the module itself, not via an onboard keyboard controller)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The keyboard column lines are coupled to Ethernet PHY pins rather than GPIOs, so keyboard scanning is likely to fail or behave unpredictably; the connections also compromise the corresponding Ethernet PHY signals.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is present: the netlist connects keyboard column outputs to pins explicitly identified as LAN_PORT1 Ethernet PHY signals, contrary to the specification's GPIO matrix wiring. This is likely to impair keyboard operation and the affected PHY signals."
}

